  <keyword>ddesd</keyword>
  <short_description>Solve delay equations with state-dependent delayed times.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>sol = ddesd(ddefun, delays, history, tspan)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>sol = ddesd(ddefun, delays, history, tspan, options)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p>
      <b>ddesd</b> solves delay equations where <b>delays(t,y)</b> returns delayed times. Constant delay vectors are interpreted as positive lags.</p>
    <table style="width:100%">
      <tr>
        <th>Item</th>
        <th>Details</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Delay type</td>
        <td>Delayed times depending on <b>t</b> and <b>y</b>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Callback</td>
        <td><b>f(t,y,z)</b></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>History</td>
        <td>Scalar, vector, solution structure, or function depending on the call form.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Solution</td>
        <td><b>sol</b> structure with <b>x</b>, <b>y</b>, <b>yp</b>, <b>solver</b>, and <b>deval</b> interpolation.</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
